 Jenkins Architecture
---------------------------------
7. What is Jenkins Controller?
The Controller is the main Jenkins server.
It manages:
Jobs
Pipelines
Credentials
Plugins
Agents
Scheduling


8. What is a Jenkins Agent?
An Agent is a machine/container that actually executes the build steps.
Jenkins Controller
       |
       | assigns job
       ↓
Jenkins Agent
       |
       └── executes build

9. Why do we use Jenkins agents?
Instead of running every build on the controller, we can distribute workloads across multiple agents.
Example:
Controller
   |
   ├── Linux Agent
   ├── Windows Agent
   └── Docker Agent


10. Controller vs Agent?
Controller	      Agent
Manages Jenkins	Executes jobs
Schedules builds	Runs build commands
Stores configuration       	Performs workload
Manages agents      	Reports results
